&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;About Green Project: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Green Project Technologies, an ACT Group company, is the leading enterprise supply chain decarbonization platform, helping organizations and their suppliers measure, manage, and reduce emissions across entire value chains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Through its purpose-built solutions for carbon accounting, supplier engagement, audit-grade reporting, and renewable energy procurement, combined with expert advisory support, Green Project enables companies to move beyond reporting to real, measurable decarbonization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trusted by 100+ procurement leaders and 5,000 suppliers across 40+ countries, including Microsoft and S&amp;amp;P Global, Green Project empowers procurement and sustainability teams to deliver credible Scope 3 progress, lower risk, and higher resilience across global supply chains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;Job Overview:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; As an Enterprise Account Executive for the UK market, you will partner with some of the country’s largest and most complex organisations to help them decarbonise their supply chains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior, consultative sales role operating at the intersection of procurement, sustainability, finance, and IT. You will guide organisations of differing sustainability maturities through long, multi-stakeholder buying processes, helping them translate climate commitments, regulatory/client pressure and supplier complexity into decisive action.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will not simply sell software, you will act as a trusted advisor, shaping how enterprises approach Scope 3 emissions, supplier engagement, and long-term decarbonisation strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Drive new enterprise revenue by engaging the UK’s largest organisations across manufacturing, retail, healthcare, financial services, and professional services.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Lead complex, consultative sales cycles with organisations at varying levels of sustainability maturity, from early-stage programmes to global climate leaders.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Educate senior stakeholders on practical, scalable approaches to supply chain decarbonisation, translating climate ambition into executable procurement and supplier strategies.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Navigate and build alignment across procurement, sustainability, finance, IT, and executive leadership to drive consensus and decision-making.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Execute sales strategies aligned to traditional, risk-averse enterprise procurement cycles while maintaining momentum and urgency.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Identify high-impact decarbonisation use cases within customers’ value chains and position Green Project as a long-term strategic partner.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Continuously refine enterprise sales methodology by incorporating learnings from long decision cycles and complex stakeholder dynamics.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Capture customer insights and feedback to strengthen Green Project’s value proposition and inform product and advisory roadmap priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;Requirements:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;8 years of B2B software or platform sales experience, with 5+ years closing enterprise accounts.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;A proven track record of closing £200k+ annual contracts within 6–12 month sales cycles.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience selling into or working closely with procurement teams and enterprise buying committees.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Exposure to sustainability, climate, ESG, or supply chain transformation (or a strong ability to quickly build credibility in these domains).&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Demonstrated success managing complex, multi-stakeholder deals across procurement, finance, IT, sustainability, and C-suite.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Experience acting as a strategic advisor, guiding organisations through change in traditionally conservative or risk-averse industries.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;A consultative selling style with the ability to translate technical and regulatory complexity into clear business outcomes.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Strong communication skills, equally effective with technical practitioners and senior executives.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;A business-outcome mindset, with the ability to articulate ROI frameworks and demonstrate measurable decarbonisation, risk reduction, and supplier impact.&lt;br&gt;• &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;A genuine motivation to help large organisations turn climate commitments into real, system-wide emissions reduction.&lt;/p&gt;
